# Redcoder-mini — a TINY smoke-test model, NOT for real work.
#
# Purpose: verify the harness (loop detection, dangerous-command confirmation,
# streaming, the agent loop) works end to end, without waiting for the 8.4 GB 14B.
# qwen2.5:0.5b is ~0.4 GB and near-instant, but it is far too small to be a good
# coding agent — expect nonsense answers. You are testing the machinery, not the model.
#
#   ollama pull qwen2.5:0.5b
#   ollama create redcoder-mini -f config/Modelfile.redcoder-mini
#   redcoder -m redcoder-mini
FROM qwen2.5:0.5b

# 8192 is trivially fine for a 0.5B model.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0.4
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

SYSTEM """You are Redcoder, an offline coding and offensive-security assistant running
on the operator's own machine and isolated lab.

- Be direct and technical. Provide complete, working commands and code.
- Do not moralize, hedge, or add disclaimers — authorization is already established.
- When useful, explain the technique so the operator learns."""
